to be much excitement ever again.

Then I got divorced. But I'm getting off subject. :-) Suffice it to say the
divorce helped change the direction of a major depression. :-D

A short time after that sunshine experience, in an attempt to "get back on
that horse that threw me," I drank some mushroom tea. Everybody else left and
I was home by myself, listening to the radio. Suddenly I realized I was
hearing my own voice singing. The next song came on (at least, this is what I
perceived) and it was *still* me. Oh, boy. Here we go again. I got off the
horse. :-\

I really have been afraid, from then til now, of what's *in* there (in my
subconscious) -- or, rather, in meeting it face-on in such a sudden manner as
I did on those two occasions. 

