put the tuna in the middle of the net. Get some high-quality cord. Tie some
cord to each of the four corners of the net. Rig some kind of pulley that you
can pull from your hiding-spot.

When the can is enjoying his wonderful MOTHERLOAD of tuna, pull the net!
(no need to pull the cat off the ground. Just make sure the net is pulled
securely.)

Be sure to tie the cord on something before you go to retrieve the cat...

